From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] proximity: check repeated vendor data before dereferencing it

The Davinci response defines repeated bytes data and required accuracy. A
protobuf message containing only accuracy therefore unpacks successfully
with n_data zero and data NULL. Check the count and pointers before reading
the first element or copying its bytes. Free the decoded message and retain
the last accepted measurement when data is absent.

Keep both existing event dispatch paths and unpack diagnostics unchanged.
This does not identify the old Uke 36-byte event or alter near/far mapping.
Reviewed against v0.4.4 and upstream main033e2a32095c024d6dbdfb1d4ae1db4a94be32f1.
Existing GPL-3.0-or-later attribution remains.

Signed-off-by: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
--- a/src/libssc-sensor-proximity.c
+++ b/src/libssc-sensor-proximity.c
@@ -106,6 +106,12 @@ report_received (SSCClient *client,
 				return;
 			}
 
+			if (msg->n_data == 0 || msg->data == NULL || msg->data->data == NULL) {
+				ssc_proximity_response_davinci__free_unpacked (msg, NULL);
+				g_warning ("Missing Xiaomi Davinci proximity data");
+				return;
+			}
+
 			if (msg->data->len != sizeof(ProximityDataDavinci)) {
 				/* Not observed and unlikely to ever happen due to reserved fields in the data struct */
 				ssc_proximity_response_davinci__free_unpacked (msg, NULL);
